        "description": "For SPY, the mean t+1 return when volume_t is ABOVE its own trailing 20-day average is HIGHER than when it is at or below it. Direction INCREASE pre-declared on the HIGH-VOLUME RETURN PREMIUM (Gervais, Kaniel & Mingelgrin 2001): securities experiencing unusually high trading volume subsequently earn higher returns, attributed to the visibility such volume confers.\n\nPre-declared caveats: (1) The original premium is CROSS-SECTIONAL on individual stocks over 1-20 day horizons. Its transfer to a single broad-index ETF is not established and may not hold at all. (2) Volume for an ETF reflects creation/redemption and hedging flow as well as directional interest, so the mechanism may not be the one documented. (3) Class balance expected to be reasonable: volume mean-reverts around its own trailing average, so both states recur by construction.",
        "expected_direction": "INCREASE",
        "hypothesis_id": "HYPOTHESIS|21384a9c-6781-49c4-a6d5-c79451551cd3",
